A||||10||CanadianGT||Fire gets my Fiero||||1||
Z||000000||CanadianGT||07-04-2001||08:34 AM||||Well I cant believe it.  I have had my 86 GT at a rebuilders for over 3 months now for a 5 day job, and it finally get's done, but a Fire ruins it.  NO , not a fire caused by my Fiero, but one that mysteriously started over the long weekend at there shop when all the mechanics were away.  I called yesterday to get my car, and he say's " we have some bad news"  "our shop went up in flames".  He says the fire departement got there in time to put it out, before my car caught fire, but instead of being red now, the entire body is black, and there is a real funky smell coming from inside.  Basically my car is ruined.  I have already paid the guy $1800 of the $3000 I owe him, and what will I get in return? A charcolled Fiero.  I have invested over $8000 in this car since I bought it 1 year and a half ago and I have nothing left.  Im only 19, and that is a lot of money to me.  On top of that I no longer have any transportation to college this fall.  The Mechanic aparently has no insurance, and I only have Liability coverage.  I think the only option I have left is to sue the guy, but even that is no guarantee.  The worst part of all this is, my Mom still has still not found out yet.  BOY AM I EVER GONNA HEAR IT!!!  On top of all that bad news about my Fiero yesterday, I come on here and the place was shut down!!  Oh well, I hope I did not bore you to much with my ranting and raving.  I guess im in the market for another Fiero now.<BR>PeAcE<BR>Kyle||||reg||1
Z||000001||Oreif||07-04-2001||09:01 AM||||Sorry to hear about your car. I hope you do not intend to pay off the rest of the $3000?<BR>Since they didn't have insurance, You could sue for the "estimated value" of the car prior to the fire.<BR>Aside from the blacked outside and the charcol smell is the rest of the car fine?<BR>Does it run? (don't know what work you were having done.) I would get the car back and see what would be needed to fix it. (body panels, interior items, etc) I would also take pics and go to another body shop and get an estimate on what it would cost to repair the car. If the first shop comes after you wanting the balance, you can have a legal defense that they need to repair the car first. I am sure the cost to repair is greater than what you owe them||||reg||9
Z||000002||CanadianGT||07-04-2001||09:36 AM||||Thanks<BR>No, I do not intend to pay off the balance of $1200 or so to the mechanics. The car does aparently run, but they were having a problem with it running to rich right after the rebuild.I am going to take your advice and go take pictures of it today.  Aparently the entire body is black, and the inside has a huge stench of smoke.  I mean there is no way even if I get it painted that anyone would want to buy a car that stinks like that, If I ever chose to sell it. That is a good idea about the legal defense, I will let my dad know.  This is such a disaster.  I guess life throws a lot of twists and turns at you, and its how you deal with them that makes you who you are.  I guess im going to find out who I am! LOL.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Ken Wittlief||07-04-2001||10:35 AM||||A chinese friend told me this story - I think its well known in China:<P>a farmers only horse ran off. All his friends came to console him. "We are so sorry to hear of your loss!"<P> the farmer said, "Who knows, maybe its a good thing".<P>  a few days later his horse came back,  with a stallion that followed it.<P>  all the farmers friends came over and said, "we are so happy at your good fortune, now you have two horses!"<P> the farmer said, "who knows, maybe its a bad thing".<P>  the stallion was a wild horse, so the farmers son tried to break it, the horse threw him and the boy broke his leg.<P>  the farmers friends all came to console the farmer, "we are so sorry your son has been injured - if you want we will destroy the horse for you".<P>  the farmer said, "dont punish the horse, who knows, maybe what happened is a good thing".<P>  a few weeks later the emperor declared war, and all the young men went off to battle, where they were outnubered and killed, except for the farmers son, who had to stay behind with his broken leg.<P>   So I guess the point is, life is a bunch of stuff that happpens, who is to say if its good or bad at the time or good or bad in the end.||||reg||11
Z||000004||Sevaan||07-04-2001||11:44 AM||||The shop will have insurance. You can sue for damages, and I highly recommend you do.||||reg||1
