Z||000007||Adrift||07-04-2001||03:54 PM||||Canadian GT - If you see you car and want to sell it, I might buy it - I won't be able to offer you much, (being even younger then you and not having a summer job!), but I've been looking for a functioning project car to rebuild cosmetically from the ground up myself.<P>Ari<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000008||KnightRyder31||07-04-2001||05:11 PM||||Life is full of small challenges...<P>Sorry about your loss.||||reg||1
Z||000009||DavidHenshaw||07-04-2001||11:45 PM||||The garage should have an insurance policy called Garage Keepers. One of the optional coverages for the owners of the garage is called Customer Car Coverage. Its possible the garage operator has no insurance.<P>Most garage buildings are rented by garage owners, hence they don't need to insure the building. However, they should all have Garage Liability and most will carry some Customer Car Coverage. Its very possible the owner will not have Customer Car Coverage or even the basic Garage Liability.<P>Bottom line, you may have to bring a legal action to discover if coverage exists. TALK TO A LAWYER. They are great in cases like this.<P>Dave<P>86 GT||||reg||1
Z||000010||Black88GT||07-05-2001||12:09 AM||||Yeah I'm with Ken.  After I got into an accident with my first Fiero I thought my life was over since the insurance company wouldnt give me anything and I had spent all my money on this car.  I began looking for another Fiero and found this 86 GT with an extra engine for only a grand, and it was sort of close!  So I borrowed a fellow MAFOA members tow dolly to get it.  The night before I went to pick it up, I notice the guy put it on ebay.  This guy was incredibly stupid and I couldnt get a straight answer out of him.  So this is great I thought, I get screwed out of a deal, and now I have this tow dolly attached to my Dads truck with nothing to do with it.  I posted my dismay to the MAFOA mailing list.  Well I got a response from a nice woman in Philadelphia about how she is considering selling her t-top GT with gold wheels and tan interior 5 speed etc. etc. etc.  I figured I couldnt afford it but she floored me with the $2000 asking price! Obviously I told her I would be there tomorrow (already had the tow dolly).  But then come to find out it needed some suspension work (actually a LOT of suspension work) so that was kind of bad.  <P>So who knows something good could come out of this like Ken pointed out.  Just thought I would share my little story to back him up.||||reg||1
